>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><em>Effective date and last updated: 10 October 2026</em></p>

  <h2 id="summary">The short version</h2>
  <p>This policy is long because the law asks us to be complete. These are the points that matter most, in plain words. Reading this summary does not replace the full policy below, which governs if anything here is unclear.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>We do not sell your data</strong> and we do not share your financial data with advertisers.</li>
    <li><strong>Some features use Google’s Gemini AI on Google’s free service tier.</strong> On that tier, Google’s terms allow Google to use what we send to improve its products, and allow human reviewers at Google to read it. This applies when you use the AI assistant, when you share a receipt image, and when our own rules cannot read a bank statement or alert you uploaded. We remove account numbers before sending where we can, but the text can still include names, amounts, merchants and dates. If you do not want this, do not use those features. We intend to move to Google’s paid tier, under which Google does not use the content to improve its products, before our public launch, and we will update this policy when we do. Section 9 has the details.</li>
    <li><strong>Bank alerts you choose to send us are read to create transactions.</strong> For accuracy, we keep the original text of alerts and statement lines you import and review, together with any corrections you make, unless you turn off “Help improve Automonie” in Settings.</li>
    <li><strong>You can see, correct, export and delete your data,</strong> and you can delete your account, which deletes your data apart from what the law requires us to keep.</li>
    <li><strong>Contact:</strong> <a href="mailto:tobe@automonie.com">tobe@automonie.com</a>. You can also complain to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission.</li>
  </ul>

